PREVIEW ONLY: This series is generated on a disposable synthesis of
Griffin Kroah-Hartman's DW9800K v4 (2026-11-19) 1/3..3/3 series,
which is under review. It is NOT based on a merged upstream commit.
Do not submit until the v4 series resolves its pending device-tree
ABI review and its final merge base is known.

The DW9800K on Surface Pro 11 uses independent 2.9 V VDD (L16B)
and 1.8 V VDDIO (PM8010 L6M). L6M is shared with the OV13858
rear sensor's DOVDD. The motor's I2C interface needs L6M powered
even when the sensor is idle; permanently pinning L6M on is not
necessary if the actuator independently votes for the rail.

This integration adds optional vddio-supply to both the generic
dw9719 binding and the v4 series' separately introduced
dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml binding. The driver enables I/O before VDD,
disables it after VDD, and unwinds it on failure; systems without
a separate supply retain their previous behavior.

SP11 OLED (X1E80100) HARDWARE TEST:
- Original pre-v4 driver + same regulator changes: passed focus writes,
  live sensor capture, 0/1/2/1/0 L6M regulator enable-count transitions,
  and four device-level PM callback cycles followed by camera use.
- v4 DW9800K driver + the same vddio change: built against this
  experimental kernel, bound to actual CCI0 master1 0x0c actuator,
  accepted positions 128/512/896/0, and switched L6M/L16B off
  after autosuspend. This module was then unloaded and the known
  test module restored.
- New v4 binding plus vddio passed dt_binding_check and
  validation of the SP11 experimental DTB. The combined v4 driver
  source on pinned mainline differs from the live-built module
  only by a pre-existing unrelated devm_kzalloc_obj conversion.

NOT CLAIMED: Optical proof of lens motion, standalone full deep system
standby, exact electrical input parent of L6M, or acceptance of
the pending DW9800K v4 series. The currently reviewed v4 series
changes DT ABI; reviewers have requested backwards compatibility.

